## Permitted use (personal, non‑commercial play)

You may use the Software without additional written permission from EidosFrontier if all of the following are true:

- your use is not for profit; and
- you do not redistribute or publicly republish the Software (or your modifications) without the rights holder’s consent.

Examples of permitted use include:

- cloning or otherwise obtaining this repository onto computers you control, then building and running it as described in the README to play, try, or evaluate the game (including visitors reviewing a portfolio who want to try it);
- reproduction strictly necessary for that purpose (such as installing dependencies); and
- letting specific friends connect only to a server you run on your own machine, or within the same private network, for multiplayer.

The following are **not** covered by this permission (separate written consent is required):

- operating the Software as an always‑on service for the general public, or hosting it so unspecified third parties can freely use it;
- publishing modified source or derivative works to a public repository without consent.

## Prohibited conduct (except as permitted above)

Without EidosFrontier’s prior written permission, you may not:

- distribute, publish, transfer, lend, sublicense, or otherwise make the Software available beyond the permitted scope;
- use the Software in commercial services or embed it in products for third parties (beyond private trial/play as described above); or
- treat the Software as freely reusable like open source without explicit consent.

Availability of the Software on GitHub permits viewing only to the extent consistent with the foregoing and does not imply consent for uses outside the permitted scope.

Any separate written agreement from the rights holder prevails.

